WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:02.294
What do we mean when we say Spartan?

00:00:02.377 --> 00:00:08.800
As an adjective, Spartan means
austere, tough, without luxury.

00:00:08.884 --> 00:00:12.554
This comes straight from the ancient
stereotype of the Spartans,

00:00:12.638 --> 00:00:15.390
the inhabitants of Sparta
in southern Greece.

00:00:15.474 --> 00:00:19.436
The Spartans were the ultimate
warriors, raised from childhood

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.064
to endure terrible suffering
and hardship.

00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:24.816
The Spartan character
is summed up perfectly

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.277
by the ancient accounts
of the Battle of Thermopylae.

00:00:27.361 --> 00:00:30.948
In 480 B.C.,
the Persians invaded Greece

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.785
and the Spartan King Leonidas,
with 300 Spartans,

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.663
held the pass against them
and died in the attempt.

00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:40.415
They didn't succeed in stopping
the Persian advance,

00:00:40.499 --> 00:00:41.917
merely slowing it down,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.127
buying precious time
for their fellow Greeks

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:45.796
and giving their lives
in the process.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:49.633
The battle exemplifies so much of
what we admire about the Spartans.

00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:52.678
Their loyalty to a cause
bigger than themselves.

00:00:52.761 --> 00:00:55.556
Their devotion to liberty and the
preservation of their homeland.

00:00:55.639 --> 00:00:59.434
In the course of their fighting
they managed a kind of grim humour,

00:00:59.518 --> 00:01:03.480
which is familiar to us today from
all sorts of action heroes whose

00:01:03.564 --> 00:01:06.859
pithy one liners are uttered at
the moment of ultimate peril.

00:01:06.942 --> 00:01:10.112
For example, when the Persians
demanded that the Spartans

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:13.615
lay down their arms,
Leonidas famously replied...

00:01:15.117 --> 00:01:18.996
Likewise, when a hail of lethal
Persian arrows blocked the sun,

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.998
Leonidas quipped to his companions...

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:27.421
We can also admire the Spartans'
association with great physical

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:29.715
fitness and toughness and endurance.

00:01:30.215 --> 00:01:33.343
In the present day they have given
their name to a particularly extreme

00:01:33.427 --> 00:01:36.805
kind of obstacle race,
which challenges people to achieve

00:01:36.889 --> 00:01:40.517
their own athletic and physical best
in the face of enormous hardship.

00:01:40.976 --> 00:01:45.439
What is more, Spartan women were just
as tough and as strong as the men.

00:01:45.814 --> 00:01:48.984
We're told by the ancient sources
that they exercised,

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:50.944
they received an education,

00:01:51.028 --> 00:01:53.739
and they were able to own
property in their own right.

00:01:54.031 --> 00:01:57.326
All things denied to the women
of other parts of Greece.

00:01:57.743 --> 00:02:01.163
However, I think there are some ways
in which we need to hesitate

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:04.082
before accepting the Spartans
as the perfect icon

00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:05.792
of our modern values today.

00:02:05.876 --> 00:02:09.254
First, they can become figureheads
of the xenophobe.

00:02:09.713 --> 00:02:13.550
The Battle of Thermopylae can start
to stand for holding out against

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.636
the encroachment of an alien invader.

00:02:15.719 --> 00:02:19.681
The most pernicious example
of the Spartans usage of this kind

00:02:19.765 --> 00:02:23.894
is in 1930s Germany, when they came
to stand for the ancestry of the

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:27.773
Aryan master race and essentially
legitimated anti-Semitism

00:02:27.856 --> 00:02:30.067
and other extreme forms
of xenophobia.

00:02:30.317 --> 00:02:34.988
Another question is whether we today
really want to claim the Spartan

00:02:35.072 --> 00:02:36.698
paradigm of masculinity.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.659
Emotion was anathema.

00:02:38.742 --> 00:02:40.327
The individual was nothing.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.287
The state was everything.

00:02:42.371 --> 00:02:47.042
As we realise more and more the need
to encourage people to express rather

00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:51.713
than deny their emotions and to show
the distress they might be feeling,

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:55.467
maybe the Spartan ideal
of masculinity is not the one

00:02:55.551 --> 00:02:57.761
we actually want to claim
for the present day.

00:02:58.095 --> 00:03:01.974
It's no coincidence that the Spartans
inspired the British public school

00:03:02.057 --> 00:03:05.143
system of the 19th
and early 20th Centuries.

00:03:05.602 --> 00:03:09.898
A system in which ideals of
discipline, endurance and austerity

00:03:09.982 --> 00:03:11.316
were paramount.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.486
Even the toughness
of Spartan women is suspect.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:18.824
The ancient sources tell us that they
trained their bodies to produce

00:03:18.907 --> 00:03:23.412
strong sons, so even the athleticism
for which they were famous

00:03:23.495 --> 00:03:26.039
serves ultimately
the Spartan war machine.

00:03:26.123 --> 00:03:29.585
And the grim joy with which they
saw their sons go to their deaths

00:03:29.668 --> 00:03:32.421
in battle is unpalatable today.

00:03:32.504 --> 00:03:36.550
Spartan women are said, by the
author Plutarch, to have told their

00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:38.218
menfolk going off to war...

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:44.516
On one's shield
of course meant dead.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:49.688
Evoking Sparta is often a way
of trying to recover values which

00:03:49.771 --> 00:03:52.566
are thought to be lost or receding.

00:03:52.649 --> 00:03:55.861
Old fashioned values
of resilience and self-denial,

00:03:55.944 --> 00:03:59.531
which some in modern society
feel that we have squandered.

00:03:59.615 --> 00:04:05.037
In fact, however, historians of
ancient Sparta have long challenged

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:09.333
the historical truthfulness of the
ancient stereotype of the Spartans.

00:04:09.416 --> 00:04:13.921
For decades now, they have been
trying to put forward an alternative

00:04:14.004 --> 00:04:17.257
Sparta with a richer,
more complex culture.

00:04:17.591 --> 00:04:21.803
Art, music and a much more
complex range of values

00:04:21.887 --> 00:04:24.181
than have traditionally been
attributed to them.

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:26.975
There is no sign however
of this happening.

00:04:27.059 --> 00:04:32.314
We are too addicted to the Spartan
stereotype, however inaccurate,

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.860
to give it up in favour of a more
complex and nuanced reality.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.060
Thanks for watching.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:45.100
Don't forget to subscribe and click the bell to receive notifications for new videos.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.520
See you again soon!

